 124:   marker â†’ nothing happens, the warm stack keeps running (the ruled default). Different or
 125:   absent marker â†’ prepare writes the config, restarts that slot's stack (`stop` + `start
 126:   --workdir`) before the reset â€” the auth container reads config at start, not at reset â€” and
 127:   writes the marker only when the restart succeeds. A crash between the write and the restart
 128:   therefore forces a restart on the next occupancy instead of hiding behind equal text.
 129: - **D4. Occupancy = the existing stack lock, extended.** `occupy()` acquires
 130:   `acquireStackLock(slotConfig, requirement)` (F3) â€” it is already the atomic create-new,
 131:   pid-stamped, stale-takeover-with-loud-line claim the ruled text describes, and it is already
