    AI4DEV-79: finish what T10 aims at - the loser must be able to READ the winner
    
    NOT RULED BY GATE 2. The executor's completion of ruling T10, in its own commit
    so one revert restores exactly the ruled text. It needs the orchestrator's
    ratification.
    
    WHAT WAS MEASURED. Ruling T10 says the create-failure catch re-reads the
    reservation and returns alreadyHeld when it names the same item. That fix is in
    the previous commit, exactly as ruled. Two concurrent reservers for one item
    were then raced on temporary directories, five rounds: ALL FIVE still ended with
    one item holding both slots.
    
    WHY. A reservation file is created exclusively and filled a moment later. In
    between it exists and cannot be read at all - the creating handle holds it with
    no sharing, so the second reader gets a sharing violation, not an empty file.
    Probed directly and confirmed. The loser is inside that window by definition; it
    lost by microseconds. So the ruled re-read saw nothing, concluded the slot
    belonged to nobody it knew, and advanced onto slot 2.
    
    THE COMPLETION. The re-read waits out the window - up to one second, thousands
    of times its length. A reservation still unreadable after the wait REJECTS this
    item rather than giving it a second slot: a false rejection is loud and costs
    one look, a silent double-take costs the whole pool of two.
    
    This is the same remedy ruling T1 applies, in this same gate, to the same window
    shape in the harness's own claim files.
    
    AFTER: eight races out of eight ended with one item holding exactly one slot,
    and the loser correctly told it already held that slot.

