 : 2026-08-09T22:04:34.121Z\npool  : C:\\Users\\nirdr\\AppData\\Local\\ai4good-build\\db-slots\n\n=== (a) preflight: every stack answers, on its own port block, BEFORE any reset ===\nslot-1    API http://127.0.0.1:55321   DB postgresql://<redacted>@127.0.0.1:55322/postgres\nslot-2    API http://127.0.0.1:56321   DB postgresql://<redacted>@127.0.0.1:56322/postgres\npersonal  API http://127.0.0.1:54321   DB postgresql://<redacted>@127.0.0.1:54322/postgres\npreflight OK: three distinct stacks, the reset target is slot-2 on 56322, and it is not the personal block.\n\n=== (b) canary row in slot-1 ===\nslot-1 canary written: [{\"note\":\"slot-1 canary\"}]\n\n=== (c) canary row in the personal stack, in a scratch schema created for this run ===\nthe scratch schema is \"ai4dev79_spike\" and it is dropped in the finally below - it is the only\nwrite this item ever makes to the personal stack.\npersonal canary written: [{\"note\":\"personal canary\"}]\n\n=== (d) canary row in slot-2 - the row the reset MUST destroy ===\nslot-2 canary written: [{\"note\":\"slot-2 canary\"}]\n\n=== (e) supabase db reset, aimed at slot-2 ===\nreset exit code: 1\n  reset: {\"_tag\":\"Error\",\"error\":{\"code\":\"LegacyGoChildExitError\",\"message\":\"failed to bootstrap the local database: exit 1\"}}\n  reset: Resetting local database...\n  reset: WARN: environment variable is unset: SUPABASE_AUTH_EXTERNAL_GITHUB_CLIENT_ID\n  reset: WARN: environment variable is unset: SUPABASE_AUTH_EXTERNAL_GITHUB_SECRET\n  reset: WARN: environment variable is unset: SUPABASE_AUTH_EXTERNAL_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID\n  reset: WARN: environment variable is unset: SUPABASE_AUTH_EXTERNAL_GOOGLE_SECRET\n  reset: Recreating database...\n  reset: failed to start docker container \"supabase_db_poancmeitlmxejofwzuu\": Error response from daemon: failed to set up container networking: driver failed programming external connectivity on endpoint supabase_db_poancmeitlmxejofwzuu (f734f404e4471e17e21da52d325a8d77ab0b119666e6434d2984647b2c5a53b7): Bind for 0.0.0.0:56322 failed: port is already allocated\n  reset: Try stopping the running project with supabase stop --project-id ai4good-slot-2\n  reset: Or configure a different db port in supabase\\config.toml\nTHE RESET FAILED. The spike cannot conclude; the canaries below are reported as they stand.\n\n=== (f) the verdict: slot-2 destroyed, slot-1 and personal surviving ===\n\n=== (g) finally: dropping the scratch schema from the personal stack ===\nTHE SCRATCH SCHEMA COULD NOT BE DROPPED. The personal stack still carries it.\nreason: no status JSON from C:\\Users\\nirdr\\Downloads\\ai4good\\.claude\\worktrees\\agent-a064eb77d7bb37dd7: \u001b[31msupabase_db_poancmeitlmxejofwzuu container is not running: created\u001b[39m\nTry rerunning the command with --debug to troubleshoot the error.\n\nMANUAL CLEANUP, run it by hand:\n  psql \"postgresql://<redacted>@127.0.0.1:54322/postgres\" -c \"drop schema if exists ai4dev79_spike cascade\"\n\n(The spike program then exited with an unhandled \"connection closed\" error, because the\ndatabase it was talking to had gone away. That stack trace is cut from this transcript; nothing\nelse was removed.)\n\nspike exit code: 1\n\n================================================================================\nPOSTSCRIPT, written by hand after the run. THE SPIKE DID NOT PROVE THE WALL.\nIT BROKE IT, AND IT DESTROYED THE FOUNDER'S LOCAL DATABASE. Read this part first.\n================================================================================\n\nWHAT HAPPENED\n\n`supabase db reset` was aimed at slot 2. It was given --workdir <slot-2> and it was run with\nits working directory set to <slot-2>. It nevertheless removed and recreated the container\nsupabase_db_poancmeitlmxejofwzuu - the founder's personal database - and it bound the new\ncontainer to 56322, which is slot 2's port. The new container could not start, because slot 2's\nown database already holds that port. The CLI said so in its own words:\n\n  failed to start docker container \"supabase_db_poancmeitlmxejofwzuu\": Bind for 0.0.0.0:56322\n  failed: port is already allocated\n  Try stopping the running project with supabase stop --project-id ai4good-slot-2\n\nOne command, two projects: the personal project's container name with slot 2's port.\n\nWHAT THE STATE IS, MEASURED AFTER THE RUN\n\n  slot-1    spike_canary = \"slot-1 canary\"   (present)\n  slot-2    spike_canary = \"slot-2 canary\"   (PRESENT - the reset destroyed nothing in slot 2)\n  personal  unreachable - its database container is in state \"created\" and does not run\n\n  docker volume supabase_db_poancmeitlmxejofwzuu  created 2026-08-09T22:04:38Z\n  docker volume supabase_storage_poancmeitlmxejofwzuu  created 2026-08-08T11:00:40Z\n  docker volume supabase_edge_runtime_poancmeitlmxejofwzuu  created 2026-08-08T11:00:41Z\n\nThe two older personal volumes are the originals. The database volume is NOT: it was created at\n22:04:38, the moment of the reset. The original database volume was deleted and an empty one put\nin its place. THE FOUNDER'S LOCAL DATABASE CONTENT IS GONE. No backup file exists anywhere in\nthe tree, and no dangling volume holds the old data. The schema itself is reproducible from\nsupabase/migrations; any rows the founder had by hand are not.\n\nThe scratch schema question is moot: the database that held it no longer exists.\n\nWHY IT HAPPENED - the root cause, measured\n\nThe tracked file `.env` at the repo root contains:\n\n  SUPABASE_PROJECT_ID=\"poancmeitlmxejofwzuu\"\n\nThe Supabase CLI treats SUPABASE_PROJECT_ID as an override of `project_id` in config.toml. It\ntherefore overrides the slot's identity while the slot's config.toml still supplies the ports.\nThe override reaches the CLI by TWO separate routes, and both must be closed:\n\n  1. through the process environment. The spike program was started by `bun spike.ts` with its\n     working directory on the repo, so bun auto-loaded the repo's `.env` into its own\n     environment, and the CLI child inherited it.\n  2. through the CLI's own working directory. The CLI reads a `.env` file from the directory it\n     runs in. This is the earlier finding recorded in the S2 setup transcript, where\n     `supabase --workdir <slot-1> status` run from the repo reported slot ports beside personal\n     containers. That was the same override arriving by the other route.\n\nTHIS IS WHY THE SETUP STEP WAS SAFE AND THE SPIKE WAS NOT. The pool's own code calls the CLI\nthrough `childEnv()`, an ALLOWLIST that does not carry SUPABASE_PROJECT_ID, and with the\nworking directory set to the slot, which has no `.env`. Both routes are closed there, which is\nwhy setup created correct slot containers. The spike script called the CLI directly and closed\nneither. The pool code was right by construction and the hand-written spike was not, so the\nspike measured the hazard instead of the wall.\n\nWHAT THIS MEANS FOR THE DESIGN\n\n--workdir is NOT the isolation mechanism. A slot is isolated only when all three agree:\nthe config it reads, the environment it runs in, and the working directory it runs from. The\nsafe form is to state the identity positively rather than merely to avoid overriding it: pass\nSUPABASE_PROJECT_ID=<the slot's project id> to every slot invocation, so the variable that\ncaused this becomes the one that enforces correctness, and add a guard that refuses when the\ncontainers the CLI would act on do not carry the slot's project id.\n\nTHE WALL IS THEREFORE UNPROVEN. This transcript is evidence of a hazard, not of isolation. The\nspike has to be run again, with the identity stated on every invocation, before anything is\nbuilt on it.\n\nEND OF S3 TRANSCRIPT\n","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":179,"totalLines":179,"truncated":false}},"title":"loop\\items\\AI4DEV-79\\spike-isolation.txt","time":{"start":1786349926444,"end":1786349926452}},"id":"prt_feac0b6fe0011zrDTuL9wn92ir","sessionID":"ses_01541a198ffeMeZOHEAs76N82N","messageID":"msg_feac0a3810011S