 the reset: project ai4good-slot-2, api 56321, db 56322\n  the line above is the helper stating which project the CLI resolved, before anything destructive.\n\n=== (f) supabase db reset, aimed at slot 2, through the helper, hostile variable present ===\ndb-pool — slot 2 identity proven before the reset: project ai4good-slot-2, api 56321, db 56322\n  the reset exited zero.\n\n=== (g) the canaries after the reset ===\n  slot 1 canary: \"slot-1 canary\"\n  slot 2 canary: null\n\n=== (h) AFTER: the same docker identity snapshot, compared on identity fields only ===\n  /supabase_analytics_poancmeitlmxejofwzuu | id 4f0cbd08610dfdd42c6c93fb9abf1eed25ecf5043bab3afa24bdad364837795d | created 2026-08-09T22:30:36.397633849Z | image public.ecr.aws/supabase/logflare:1.47.1 | ports {\"4000/tcp\":[{\"HostIp\":\"\",\"HostPort\":\"54327\"}]}\n  /supabase_auth_poancmeitlmxejofwzuu | id 38d058a45856033b6715edbb78b4fce73392283ff9930e9043fe490031d324f0 | created 2026-08-09T22:30:38.180055558Z | image public.ecr.aws/supabase/gotrue:v2.193.0 | ports {}\n  /supabase_db_poancmeitlmxejofwzuu | id a9fc53b713132db35df62f08563a31552eb93662efd925e6e35efe19b9e7c588 | created 2026-08-09T22:30:25.016886496Z | image public.ecr.aws/supabase/postgres:17.6.1.143 | ports {\"5432/tcp\":[{\"HostIp\":\"\",\"HostPort\":\"54322\"}]}\n  /supabase_inbucket_poancmeitlmxejofwzuu | id 05a41d3f900184d874744b3f69099877ddcaad0facc5cdedeab768acb03e6937 | created 2026-08-09T22:30:38.737406565Z | image public.ecr.aws/supabase/mailpit:v1.30.2 | ports {\"8025/tcp\":[{\"HostIp\":\"\",\"HostPort\":\"54324\"}]}\n  /supabase_kong_poancmeitlmxejofwzuu | id c60a42f259068af05d0cffe4a8a2e21e49378fe644d69c1d0a144c747a20ba10 | created 2026-08-09T22:30:37.447243163Z | image public.ecr.aws/supabase/kong:2.8.1 | ports {\"8000/tcp\":[{\"HostIp\":\"\",\"HostPort\":\"54321\"}]}\n  /supabase_pg_meta_poancmeitlmxejofwzuu | id dd9e8be3bb873f596ff92236e3d604ac10303cd5da8c5227e50e7b9f6d54dafd | created 2026-08-09T22:30:41.700396649Z | image public.ecr.aws/supabase/postgres-meta:v0.96.6 | ports {}\n  /supabase_realtime_poancmeitlmxejofwzuu | id e1a443bf280ab38ab8bf6cfdc3947bda9540f0fda03557188b94d50a0ca75f2b | created 2026-08-09T22:30:39.298314473Z | image public.ecr.aws/supabase/realtime:v2.113.4 | ports {}\n  /supabase_rest_poancmeitlmxejofwzuu | id 720fc47910c49a2e12f0b6ef8386a29b651ed61ba01611aad962c580f2a798ef | created 2026-08-09T22:30:39.873216866Z | image public.ecr.aws/supabase/postgrest:v14.15 | ports {}\n  /supabase_storage_poancmeitlmxejofwzuu | id e38f52bfb2c2b847d7b28db03b04c921cfaef24e4e680b25feb940a1ebb156ea | created 2026-08-09T22:30:40.509213548Z | image public.ecr.aws/supabase/storage-api:v1.66.4 | ports {}\n  /supabase_studio_poancmeitlmxejofwzuu | id 0f2789d632ab074db933abb784b8e148b1f9b8fd86c5b74918bf45e767ec170a | created 2026-08-09T22:30:42.329002909Z | image public.ecr.aws/supabase/studio:2026.07.13-sha-b5ada96 | ports {\"3000/tcp\":[{\"HostIp\":\"\",\"HostPort\":\"54323\"}]}\n  /supabase_vector_poancmeitlmxejofwzuu | id 54f791bf65decc8744a68ca032ec8ce195fd9cf88e1b225d29a48bef91ab18bb | created 2026-08-09T22:30:36.96867758Z | image public.ecr.aws/supabase/vector:0.53.0-alpine | ports {}\n  supabase_db_poancmeitlmxejofwzuu | created 2026-08-09T22:25:17Z\n  supabase_edge_runtime_poancmeitlmxejofwzuu | created 2026-08-08T11:00:41Z\n  supabase_storage_poancmeitlmxejofwzuu | created 2026-08-08T11:00:40Z\n  IDENTICAL: same container ids, created timestamps, images, port bindings, volumes and volume CreatedAt.\n\n=== the done-criterion, item by item ===\n  PASS  the hostile variable was present in the parent process\n  PASS  the identity pre-read named slot 2 before the reset\n  PASS  the reset ran through the helper and exited zero\n  PASS  the slot 2 canary is GONE — the reset acted on slot 2\n  PASS  the slot 1 canary SURVIVES — the reset acted on nothing else\n  PASS  the personal docker snapshots are equal on every identity field\n\nTHE SPIKE PASSED: the wall holds under the exact condition that broke it.\n\nResidue: slot 1 keeps a public.spike_canary table until its next occupancy, which resets it.\nEND OF S3 TRANSCRIPT (re-proof)\n\n================================================================================\nPOSTSCRIPT, written by hand after the run.\n================================================================================\n\nTHE TREE THE RUN USED. The head line above says 3ca44eb, which was the last\ncommit at the moment of the run. The working tree also carried one uncommitted\nedit: writeCanary drops and recreates its table instead of using CREATE TABLE IF\nNOT EXISTS. Both are in the commit that carries this transcript.\n\nTHE FIRST ATTEMPT, recorded because a transcript that hides one is not evidence.\nThe spike was run once before this run and stopped at step (c) with:\n\n  null value in column \"id\" of relation \"spike_canary\" violates not-null constraint\n\nSlot 1 still held a spike_canary table left by the first, failed spike of\n2026-08-09, with a column set of its own. CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS therefore\ncreated nothing and the insert failed on that table's constraint. The stop was a\ncanary client problem in a slot database. No identity was resolved, no CLI\ncommand ran after the preflight reads, and step (h) of that attempt already\nreported the personal docker snapshot IDENTICAL. The fix was to drop and\nrecreate the canary table, and the run above is the re-run.\n\nTWO INDEPENDENT READS AGREE THAT THE PERSONAL STACK WAS NOT TOUCHED. Step (h)\ncompares the docker identity snapshot and reports it identical. A separate\ndocker ps taken after the run reports every personal container still up with the\nsame uptime it had before the run, so nothing recreated or restarted one. The\ntracked .env is byte for byte unchanged, verified by SHA-256 before and after.\n\nEND OF POSTSCRIPT","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":119,"totalLines":119,"truncated":false}},"title":"loop\\items\\AI4DEV-79\\spike-isolation-2.txt","time":{"start"