ore the reset: project ai4good-slot-2, api 56321, db 56322\n55:   the reset exited zero.\n56: \n57: === (g) the canaries after the reset ===\n58:   slot 1 canary: \"slot-1 canary\"\n59:   slot 2 canary: null\n60: \n61: === (h) AFTER: the same docker identity snapshot, compared on identity fields only ===\n62:   /supabase_analytics_poancmeitlmxejofwzuu | id 4f0cbd08610dfdd42c6c93fb9abf1eed25ecf5043bab3afa24bdad364837795d | created 2026-08-09T22:30:36.397633849Z | image public.ecr.aws/supabase/logflare:1.47.1 | ports {\"4000/tcp\":[{\"HostIp\":\"\",\"HostPort\":\"54327\"}]}\n63:   /supabase_auth_poancmeitlmxejofwzuu | id 38d058a45856033b6715edbb78b4fce73392283ff9930e9043fe490031d324f0 | created 2026-08-09T22:30:38.180055558Z | image public.ecr.aws/supabase/gotrue:v2.193.0 | ports {}\n64:   /supabase_db_poancmeitlmxejofwzuu | id a9fc53b713132db35df62f08563a31552eb93662efd925e6e35efe19b9e7c588 | created 2026-08-09T22:30:25.016886496Z | image public.ecr.aws/supabase/postgres:17.6.1.143 | ports {\"5432/tcp\":[{\"HostIp\":\"\",\"HostPort\":\"54322\"}]}\n65:   /supabase_inbucket_poancmeitlmxejofwzuu | id 05a41d3f900184d874744b3f69099877ddcaad0facc5cdedeab768acb03e6937 | created 2026-08-09T22:30:38.737406565Z | image public.ecr.aws/supabase/mailpit:v1.30.2 | ports {\"8025/tcp\":[{\"HostIp\":\"\",\"HostPort\":\"54324\"}]}\n66:   /supabase_kong_poancmeitlmxejofwzuu | id c60a42f259068af05d0cffe4a8a2e21e49378fe644d69c1d0a144c747a20ba10 | created 2026-08-09T22:30:37.447243163Z | image public.ecr.aws/supabase/kong:2.8.1 | ports {\"8000/tcp\":[{\"HostIp\":\"\",\"HostPort\":\"54321\"}]}\n67:   /supabase_pg_meta_poancmeitlmxejofwzuu | id dd9e8be3bb873f596ff92236e3d604ac10303cd5da8c5227e50e7b9f6d54dafd | created 2026-08-09T22:30:41.700396649Z | image public.ecr.aws/supabase/postgres-meta:v0.96.6 | ports {}\n68:   /supabase_realtime_poancmeitlmxejofwzuu | id e1a443bf280ab38ab8bf6cfdc3947bda9540f0fda03557188b94d50a0ca75f2b | created 2026-08-09T22:30:39.298314473Z | image public.ecr.aws/supabase/realtime:v2.113.4 | ports {}\n69:   /supabase_rest_poancmeitlmxejofwzuu | id 720fc47910c49a2e12f0b6ef8386a29b651ed61ba01611aad962c580f2a798ef | created 2026-08-09T22:30:39.873216866Z | image public.ecr.aws/supabase/postgrest:v14.15 | ports {}\n70:   /supabase_storage_poancmeitlmxejofwzuu | id e38f52bfb2c2b847d7b28db03b04c921cfaef24e4e680b25feb940a1ebb156ea | created 2026-08-09T22:30:40.509213548Z | image public.ecr.aws/supabase/storage-api:v1.66.4 | ports {}\n71:   /supabase_studio_poancmeitlmxejofwzuu | id 0f2789d632ab074db933abb784b8e148b1f9b8fd86c5b74918bf45e767ec170a | created 2026-08-09T22:30:42.329002909Z | image public.ecr.aws/supabase/studio:2026.07.13-sha-b5ada96 | ports {\"3000/tcp\":[{\"HostIp\":\"\",\"HostPort\":\"54323\"}]}\n72:   /supabase_vector_poancmeitlmxejofwzuu | id 54f791bf65decc8744a68ca032ec8ce195fd9cf88e1b225d29a48bef91ab18bb | created 2026-08-09T22:30:36.96867758Z | image public.ecr.aws/supabase/vector:0.53.0-alpine | ports {}\n73:   supabase_db_poancmeitlmxejofwzuu | created 2026-08-09T22:25:17Z\n74:   supabase_edge_runtime_poancmeitlmxejofwzuu | created 2026-08-08T11:00:41Z\n75:   supabase_storage_poancmeitlmxejofwzuu | created 2026-08-08T11:00:40Z\n76:   IDENTICAL: same container ids, created timestamps, images, port bindings, volumes and volume CreatedAt.\n77: \n78: === the done-criterion, item by item ===\n79:   PASS  the hostile variable was present in the parent process\n80:   PASS  the identity pre-read named slot 2 before the reset\n81:   PASS  the reset ran through the helper and exited zero\n82:   PASS  the slot 2 canary is GONE — the reset acted on slot 2\n83:   PASS  the slot 1 canary SURVIVES — the reset acted on nothing else\n84:   PASS  the personal docker snapshots are equal on every identity field\n85: \n86: THE SPIKE PASSED: the wall holds under the exact condition that broke it.\n87: \n88: Residue: slot 1 keeps a public.spike_canary table until its next occupancy, which resets it.\n89: END OF S3 TRANSCRIPT (re-proof)\n90: \n91: ================================================================================\n92: POSTSCRIPT, written by hand after the run.\n93: ================================================================================\n94: \n95: THE TREE THE RUN USED. The head line above says 3ca44eb, which was the last\n96: commit at the moment of the run. The working tree also carried one uncommitted\n97: edit: writeCanary drops and recreates its table instead of using CREATE TABLE IF\n98: NOT EXISTS. Both are in the commit that carries this transcript.\n99: \n100: THE FIRST ATTEMPT, recorded because a transcript that hides one is not evidence.\n101: The spike was run once before this run and stopped at step (c) with:\n102: \n103:   null value in column \"id\" of relation \"spike_canary\" violates not-null constraint\n104: \n105: Slot 1 still held a spike_canary table left by the first, failed spike of\n106: 2026-08-09, with a column set of its own. CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS therefore\n107: created nothing and the insert failed on that table's constraint. The stop was a\n108: canary client problem in a slot database. No identity was resolved, no CLI\n109: command ran after the preflight reads, and step (h) of that attempt already\n110: reported the personal docker snapshot IDENTICAL. The fix was to drop and\n111: recreate the canary table, and the run above is the re-run.\n112: \n113: TWO INDEPENDENT READS AGREE THAT THE PERSONAL STACK WAS NOT TOUCHED. Step (h)\n114: compares the docker identity snapshot and reports it identical. A separate\n115: docker ps taken after the run reports every personal container still up with the\n116: same uptime it had before the run, so nothing recreated or restarted one. The\n117: tracked .env is byte for byte unchanged, verified by SHA-256 before and after.\n118: \n119: END OF POSTSCRIPT\n\n(End of file - total 119 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"\nAI4DEV-79 (parallel DB slot pool) - step S3 as amended by ruling E5, the i