ct; the working directory stops anything\\n53: else from claiming to be one. The first setup attempt on this machine ran with the working\\n54: directory on the repo: supabase start found the personal database container healthy, decided\\n55: the project was already running, and exited zero having created no slot container at all.\\n56: \\n57: === the personal stack, read BEFORE setup (a read; nothing is written to it) ===\\n58: Stopped services: [supabase_imgproxy_poancmeitlmxejofwzuu supabase_pooler_poancmeitlmxejofwzuu]\\n59: {\\\"DB_URL\\\":\\\"postgresql://<redacted>@127.0.0.1:54322/postgres\\\",\\\"API_URL\\\":\\\"http://127.0.0.1:54321\\\",\\\"REST_URL\\\":\\\"http://127.0.0.1:54321/rest/v1\\\",\\\"GRAPHQL_URL\\\":\\\"http://127.0.0.1:54321/graphql/v1\\\",\\\"FUNCTIONS_URL\\\":\\\"http://127.0.0.1:54321/functions/v1\\\",\\\"MCP_URL\\\":\\\"http://127.0.0.1:54321/mcp\\\",\\\"STUDIO_URL\\\":\\\"http://127.0.0.1:54323\\\",\\\"PUBLISHABLE_KEY\\\":\\\"<redacted-key>\\\",\\\"SECRET_KEY\\\":\\\"<redacted-key>\\\",\\\"JWT_SECRET\\\":\\\"<redacted>\\\",\\\"ANON_KEY\\\":\\\"<redacted-jwt>\\\",\\\"SERVICE_ROLE_KEY\\\":\\\"<redacted-jwt>\\\",\\\"MAILPIT_URL\\\":\\\"http://127.0.0.1:54324\\\",\\\"INBUCKET_URL\\\":\\\"http://127.0.0.1:54324\\\",\\\"STORAGE_S3_URL\\\":\\\"http://127.0.0.1:54321/storage/v1/s3\\\",\\\"S3_PROTOCOL_ACCESS_KEY_ID\\\":\\\"<redacted>\\\",\\\"S3_PROTOCOL_ACCESS_KEY_SECRET\\\":\\\"<redacted>\\\",\\\"S3_PROTOCOL_REGION\\\":\\\"local\\\",\\\"message\\\":\\\"\\\"}\\n60: \\n61: === removing the two slot directories left by the first, failed attempt ===\\n62: slot-1 present after removal: False\\n63: slot-2 present after removal: False\\n64: containers named for a slot before setup: \\n65: \\n66: === bun tests/at/harness/db-pool.ts setup ===\\n67: db-pool setup — pool root C:\\\\Users\\\\nirdr\\\\AppData\\\\Local\\\\ai4good-build\\\\db-slots\\n68: db-pool setup — source configuration C:\\\\Users\\\\nirdr\\\\Downloads\\\\ai4good\\\\.claude\\\\worktrees\\\